<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Retribution Paladin</span></h2>Crafted items are, for the most part, bind-on-equip - meaning you don't need to be any specific profession in order to gain access to them. One exception to this rule is the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> which requires Engineering.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94266/haunted-steel-greathelm">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Greathelm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Greathelm</span></a> - a 522 item level helmet pre-upgrade that is craftable with the new reagents available in Phase 3, and in a vacuum will be better than anything available outside of raid.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94267/haunted-steel-warboots">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Warboots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_deathknight_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Warboots</span></a> - a 522 item level pair of boots pre-upgrade that is craftable with the new reagents available in Phase 3, and in a vacuum will be better than anything available outside of raid.<br/>
<span class="small-text">If you need the Hit, then choose these over the Treads.</span></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94265/haunted-steel-treads">
<img alt="Haunted Steel Treads" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raidwarrior_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haunted Steel Treads</span></a> - a 522 item level pair of boots pre-upgrade that is craftable with the new reagents available in Phase 3, and in a vacuum will be better than anything available outside of raid.<br/>
<span class="small-text">If you don't need the Hit, then choose these over the Warboots.</span></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77539/reinforced-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Reinforced Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Retinal Armor</span></a> - the only bind-on-pickup crafted item, which requires Engineering, and is one of the more potent crafted items available; especially notable when you first reach max level. Due to the powerful cogwheel gems that can be slotted in, it is a popular choice for Challenge Mode content where gems avoid the downward scaling.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a> - high item-level gloves crafted by Blacksmiths with a recipe obtained inside of raids, outclassed only by raid items.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82975/ghost-reavers-breastplate">
<img alt="Ghost Reaver's Breastplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Reaver's Breastplate</span></a> - a really solid pre-raid chestpiece crafted by Blacksmiths. The pattern requires <span class="rep-honored">Honored</span> with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1337/the-klaxxi">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Klaxxi</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=82976/ghost-reavers-gauntlets">
<img alt="Ghost Reaver's Gauntlets" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_plate_reputation_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ghost Reaver's Gauntlets</span></a> - another solid pre-raid pair of gloves crafted by Blacksmiths, with a pattern requiring <span class="rep-honored">Honored</span> with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1337/the-klaxxi">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Klaxxi</span></a>. However, notably weaker than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=87407/bloodforged-warfists">
<img alt="Bloodforged Warfists" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlet_plate_raidwarrior_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodforged Warfists</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_priest_angelicfeather.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Retribution Paladin Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>Trinkets for Paladin DPS are rather straightforward as you will usually be selecting the trinkets with the highest item level, narrowed down to the trinkets that provide the most favorable stats - following our stat priority. Active trinkets should be used on cooldown as much as possible, unless aligned with specific boss damage taken increasing mechanics. They should also be stacked with &amp; overlap the duration of your class cooldowns, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=31884/avenging-wrath">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_avenginewrath.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Avenging Wrath</span></a>, whenever possible.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Paladins should be wearing no more than one active on-use trinket, as two active trinkets cannot be stacked at the same time and will share a short cooldown preventing their effects from overlapping. Two passive trinkets, however, is completely fine, and we will often use two passive trinkets together as they are much more common in Mists of Pandaria. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81268/lessons-of-the-darkmaster">
<img alt="Lessons of the Darkmaster" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lessons of the Darkmaster</span></a> is the strongest trinket from heroic dungeons and can even compete against slightly higher iLvl epic trinkets due to its itemization.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86042/jade-charioteer-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Charioteer Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_mount_ridinghorse.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Charioteer Figurine</span></a> is a rather weak option due to the short 1-min cooldown that won't often overlap with our class cooldowns - all of the epic passive trinkets are better, as is <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81268/lessons-of-the-darkmaster">
<img alt="Lessons of the Darkmaster" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lessons of the Darkmaster</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89083/iron-belly-wok">
<img alt="Iron Belly Wok" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_cooking_masterofthewok.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Iron Belly Wok</span></a> is completely identical to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86042/jade-charioteer-figurine">
<img alt="Jade Charioteer Figurine" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_mount_ridinghorse.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jade Charioteer Figurine</span></a>, instead requiring reputation with the <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1270/shado-pan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shado-Pan</span></a> and some <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=93261/helmbreaker-medallion">
<img alt="Helmbreaker Medallion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Helmbreaker Medallion</span></a> /<wbr/> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=93256/skullrender-medallion">
<img alt="Skullrender Medallion" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skullrender Medallion</span></a> - these trinkets are available from <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1376/operation-shieldwall">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Operation: Shieldwall</span></a> or <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1375/dominance-offensive">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dominance Offensive</span></a> reputation, depending on what faction you play. While they provide valuable passive Strength, the Critical Strike Chance on-use effect is not one of our preferred stats, making this trinket fall behind passive trinkets of a similar item level.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95726/fabled-feather-of-ji-kun">
<img alt="Fabled Feather of Ji-Kun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_priest_angelicfeather.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fabled Feather of Ji-Kun</span></a> - One of our best-in-slot trinkets in Phase 3, this is from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>, however this Celestial version can be acquired with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=3350/august-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="August Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendarygem_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">August Stone Fragment</span></span></a> and is pre-raid best-in-slot once it becomes available.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> - This trinket is acquired from <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1435/shado-pan-assault">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> reputation and <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>, and can be upgraded to 530 iLvl without entering a raid - which will only be beat by the fully upgraded or thunderforged <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96873/primordius-talisman-of-rage">
<img alt="Primordius' Talisman of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordius' Talisman of Rage</span></a> with 541 iLvl.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95757/primordius-talisman-of-rage">
<img alt="Primordius' Talisman of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordius' Talisman of Rage</span></a> - Another strong option from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>, this Celestial version however can be purchased with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/currency=3350/august-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="August Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendarygem_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">August Stone Fragment</span></span></a> after the release of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a>. Unless you acquire the 541 iLvl variant of this trinket, it will be beat by an upgraded <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79327/relic-of-xuen">
<img alt="Relic of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_tiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Xuen</span></a> is obtainable before entering any raids via the Darkmoon Faire <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79323/tiger-deck">
<img alt="Tiger Deck" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_deck_whitetiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tiger Deck</span></a> and can be upgraded to iLvl 484, making it pre-raid best-in-slot before the release of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6622/throne-of-thunder">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Throne of Thunder</span></a> and its respective Celestial trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86802/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a> was one of our best in slot trinkets in Phases 1-2, and is obtained from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6125/mogushan-vaults">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Mogu'shan Vaults</span></a>. The Celestial variant is easily acquired before entering raids. This trinket will pull slightly ahead of the Celestial variant of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86894/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86894/darkmist-vortex">
<img alt="Darkmist Vortex" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_cyclone_nodebris.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Darkmist Vortex</span></a> was one of our best in slot trinkets in Phases 1-2, and is obtained from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6067/terrace-of-endless-spring">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Terrace of Endless Spring</span></a>. The Celestial variant is easily acquired before entering raids, though falls slightly behind the Celestial variant of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86802/lei-shens-final-orders">
<img alt="Lei Shen's Final Orders" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lei Shen's Final Orders</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Retribution Paladin</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, the Hit &amp; Expertise caps will change slightly to 7.5% Hit and 7.5% Expertise when dealing damage against raid-level bosses. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_human_female.gif");'></span>
<b>Human</b> racial passive <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=20597/sword-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_meleedamage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sword Specialization</span></a>, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise, reducing the amount needed from gear &amp; reforging.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, our abilities and melee swings will no longer miss raid bosses <i>(+3 levels above you)</i>. When our attacks miss, we do not generate <a data-entity="resource" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/resource/holy-power-9">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Power</span></a> or trigger <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=31801/seal-of-truth">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_sealofvengeance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of Truth</span></a>, so it is very important to be Hit capped.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, our abilities and melee swings will no longer be dodged by raid bosses <i>(+3 levels above you)</i>. They can still parry our attacks if they are facing us, but we will almost always try to be behind them in order to avoid parries, as mobs cannot parry attacks from behind. When our attacks dodge or parry, we do not generate <a data-entity="resource" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/resource/holy-power-9">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Power</span></a> or trigger <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=31801/seal-of-truth">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_sealofvengeance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of Truth</span></a>, so it is very important to be Expertise capped.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Retribution Paladin</span></h2>We will generally prioritize stacking as much haste as possible, therefore we will primarily be using <span class="c4">Yellow</span>, <span class="c11">Orange</span>, or <span class="c3">Green</span> gems to complete our socket bonuses. It is generally worth going for every socket bonus, because we have strong haste gems we can use for any specific color. We will also utilize <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a> if we can make use of the expertise, otherwise stick to <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76669/fierce-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Fierce Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fierce Vermilion Onyx</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>We will also use one single <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a> in the full best-in-slot set, due to reaching a breakpoint on haste.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="q9">Meta Gem</span>: <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76886/reverberating-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_metagem_cut.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Primal Diamond</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c4">Yellow Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76699/quick-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Quick Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Sun's Radiance</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c11">Orange Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a> &gt; <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76669/fierce-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Fierce Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fierce Vermilion Onyx</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c9">Purple Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76684/etched-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Etched Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Imperial Amethyst</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="c3">Green Gem</span>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76642/lightning-wild-jade">
<img alt="Lightning Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Wild Jade</span></a></div></li></ul>
